<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial dips on merger speculation.</title>
<headline>Commercial dips on merger speculation.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial Bank Ltd fell six percent, or eight rupees, to 125 on Friday on news that Hatton National Bank Ltd has offered 103 rupees a share for a stake in the bank, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's report in the Island newspaper that HNB has offered only 103 rupees a share, is putting downward pressure on Commercial Bank shares,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank said on Thursday that Hatton National and Development Finance Corp of Ceylon Ltd, had expressed interest in buying 40 percent of its capital, currently held by Standard Chartered Bank Plc.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
